        "note": "SUBJECTIVE\n\nNot provided.\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nVital Signs: Blood pressure 128/76 mmHg.\n\nPhysical Examination: Faint crackles at the right base. Urinalysis negative, no nitrites.\n\nTESTING RESULTS\n\nUrinalysis: negative, no nitrites.\n\nASSESSMENT\n\nPatient is a 71-year-old female with no past medical history documented in the available records who presented with community-acquired pneumonia. She was admitted and initiated on ceftriaxone. Now on day 3 of ceftriaxone therapy, she remains afebrile overnight with improving cough. Physical examination reveals faint crackles at the right base, consistent with ongoing pneumonic process. Urinalysis is negative. Overall clinical trajectory supports continued inpatient management with current antibiotic therapy and close monitoring for clinical response.\n\nPLAN\n\n1. Continue intravenous ceftriaxone for community-acquired pneumonia; obtain repeat chest X-ray tomorrow morning to assess radiographic response.\n\n2. Restart metoprolol tartrate 25 mg PO BID.\n\n3. Assess for dysuria at the afternoon visit.",
